PETEY BENCHMARK HEURISTICS AND GLOSSARY

The Petey Benchmark (name TBD) measures a tool's ability to identify Fields in a PDF, as well as the Field's Type and the other fields in the document it is associated with. The documents are flat PDFs with their metadata removed, so this task must be accomplished strictly with what is printed on the page.

FIELDS
The basic unit of this data set is the Field. A Field is any place on a form that information is supposed to go. It is defined by its location and its Type.

TYPES OF FIELDS
Text
A Text Field contains text, whether it is a two-letter state code or several paragraphs. 

Choice
A Choice Field is a boolean switch, usually a checkbox or a radio button. While these two function differently in practice, they are equivalent in this context.

Signature
A Signature Field is anywhere that a person is supposed to sign their name or initial.

--

COLLECTIONS
Mltiple fields that are associated are called a Collection.

TYPES OF COLLECTIONS
There are four types of Collections: Groups, Entities, Grids and Blocks. A Field can only be a member of a single Group or Entity. The same goes for Grids and Blocks, with the caveat that Groups and Entities function like single Fields within a Grid or Block. 
 
Groups
A Group is a collection of associated Choice Fields.

Entities
An Entity is a collection of Text Fields that appear sequentially on a single line that comprise a single value. These values are limited to common values like dates, telephone numbers, addresses, and ID codes.

Grids
A Grid is a collection of Fields arranged in discrete rows and columns, where each row and column has a unique identifier. Not every position in the Grid needs to have a Field, and it's not uncommon for some columns to not apply to some rows. 

Blocks
A Block is an arrangement of equivalent Fields that recurs across the document. Each unique arrangement within a document is called a Block Type. Types are defined by a mix of relative positions and labels (indicated by the text layer of the document). Blocks of the same Type can differ in their exact fields and their exact arrangement, within set tolerances.

